{
  "version": 1,
  "_comment": [
    "Orlok's gesture vocabulary (GESTURE-ENGINE-SPEC.md §7.1), authored against the",
    "hardware that is ACTUALLY available on this node as of 2026-08-16, not the full",
    "instrument the spec imagines:",
    "  part 15  Head on a Swivel  — working, calibrated 60-120",
    "  part 8   Hand of Azura     — working relay light",
    "  part 5   Forearm Rotation  — allowed, 95-125, shares the 'arm-fused-rail'",
    "  part 4   Elbow             — BLOCKED, servo physically failed",
    "  part 3   Bow At The Waist  — BLOCKED, ambiguous BTS7960 wiring",
    "So every recipe here is built on head + light, the two reliably working parts,",
    "with the forearm added where a second servo earns its keep. The bow-dependent",
    "gestures (courtly_bow, kiss_bow) are expressed as head bows: honest about the",
    "hardware rather than commanding a blocked actuator and calling it a bow. When",
    "the elbow and bow are repaired, deepen them here — do not add new parts to a",
    "step window that already contains part 5 (same fused rail)."
  ],
